/-!
# Checked square coordinates for outside-C pruning

Collect the square of an arbitrary positive split F₄ word. The two initial
coordinates remove the first B₂ block when X₈ is nonzero. On the normalized
slice, three further coordinates remove X₅, X₂ and Y₃. Each exchange uses
the proved matrix root relations, and detection uses split-word injectivity.
The adjacent source/generate.py is an untrusted proof-writing tool.

Source: GLS3 Table 2.4 and 2.4.5(d), refs/KGroup/GLS3/chapter2.tex.
-/

public section
noncomputable section
